Setup modal mobile looks good, fits without scroll. Great. Note selected opponent RAVEN, difficulty "THƯỜNG" not "DỄ" because when selecting RAVEN default difficulty? setupCtx.team default raven and difficulty normal. But raven's difficulty easy. When user clicks opponent it sets difficulty. On open, team raven but difficulty normal (mismatch). In data, OPPONENTS[0] raven easy. The default setup currently team "raven", difficulty "normal", so default should maybe be easy? The user can pick. Could adjust `openSetup` default difficulty to opponent difficulty for team. But current UI shows opponent Raven selected but difficulty "THƯỜNG", which is inconsistent with Raven label "Dễ". Maybe intended the user can choose any difficulty independent of team. The setup UI shows opponent label "Dễ" next to Raven, and difficulty independently. But selecting opponent auto-sets difficulty. So at open there's inconsistency. Better set default team maybe "atlas" normal, or default difficulty easy. Simpler: when mode quick and no explicit opts, set team "raven" and difficulty "easy" (matching). Or default to atlas/normal. The home hero says "ĐÁ NHANH" and quick match. Most users expect normal. Could default team "atlas" (Thường) so difficulty normal matches. But opponent default in setupCtx is raven. Changing to atlas would be fine; or set default difficulty to OPPONENTS.find raven.difficulty = easy. Then UI selected "DỄ" and Raven. I think easiest: after setting team, if no opts.difficulty and !fixed, set difficulty from selected opponent. But openSetup opts default may be `opts.difficulty || "normal"`; we can set default to mapping. Code:

```
setupCtx = {
 mode: opts.mode || "quick",
 team: opts.team || "raven",
 difficulty: opts.difficulty || "normal",
 fixed: !!opts.fixed
};
if (!opts.fixed && !opts.difficulty) {
 const o = D.OPPONENTS.find(x => x.team === setupCtx.team);
 if (o) setupCtx.difficulty = o.difficulty;
}
```
This sets easy for raven. That is consistent. But maybe quick match default should be normal. We can instead default team atlas. Hmm. "RAVEN FC · Dễ" is the first choice. It's okay to start easy. Better for new players.

Alternatively leave as is; not a bug. But UI mismatch might confuse: opponent says Dễ, difficulty "THƯỜNG". Let's fix with mapping.

Also in screenshot, the modal close button is a dark square at top right, fine. Bottom fine print line is tiny but okay. The "ĐỘ KHÓ" button labels fit.

Let's patch openSetup default difficulty mapping.

